<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids weaken on sales.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids weaken on sales.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat turned weaker Wednesday and Thursday, grain merchandisers in the U.S. High Plains said.</p>
<p>Dealers said bids were weakening as farmers took advantage of higher prices to sell some of their wheat.</p>
<p>&quot;Farmers have definitely surrendered some wheat -- I'd say we've bought over 100,000 bushels over the last two to three days,&quot; a central Kansas merchandiser said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, there were rumblings about a large winter snowstorm arriving next week in western Kansas.</p>
<p>One wheat futures broker said a private weather forecaster in Kansas City was expecting at least 18 inches of snow in southwest Kansas early next week.  </p>
